WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.170
Click Alignments in the sidebar.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.730
The demo workspace includes six saved
examples.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.130
Open Synthetic Sanger, primer pair and
overlapping reads.

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.290
This example contains a twelve-hundred-base
template and two overlapping

5
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.290
reads, each with eight hundred base calls.

6
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.090
Expand the alignment to fill the workspace.

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.010
The rows keep the template and reads in a
common coordinate view.

8
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.430
Click Next mismatch to jump to a difference
instead of searching through

9
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.580
every column. Compare the letters in the
highlighted region with the surrounding

10
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.650
trace peaks and consensus row.

11
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.970
Return from the filled alignment view, then
click Open chromatogram.

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.730
The original read opens with its base
calls, colored peaks, and quality

13
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.170
information. Use the read name to confirm
which trace you are reviewing.

14
00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:53.170
The trace panel also reports retained calls
at the selected quality threshold.

15
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.710
You can move between this original-read
view and the saved alignment when

16
00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.162
checking a discrepancy.
